text:
maya.l: Hey folks — seeing missing child spans from our Java batch Kafka worker. Root span (consumer.process) shows up but downstream spans from processing tasks often absent. Happens ~30% of traces when batch size > 50. Otel Java agent v1.30 attached. Any suggestions where to look?

rajiv.k: do you see trace ids in the task logs at all? sounds like context propagation across threads may be dropping. are you using executor.submit without wrapping?

maya.l: sometimes trace-id printed in worker logs, sometimes blank. We submit tasks with ExecutorService.submit(() -> process(record)) and also use CompletableFuture.supplyAsync for enrichment calls. We get tracer via GlobalOpenTelemetry.getTracer("batch-worker"). No explicit Context.wrap right now.

sasha: very likely executor context loss. quick try: wrap Runnables/Callables with Context.current().wrap(...) or use the Java agent's auto-instrumentation for executors. Also check your kafka client instrumentation — if you manually start a span in the poll loop but then immediately fire async work without making it current, child spans won't join.

rajiv.k: quick checklist to debug: 1) confirm -javaagent is attached (ps or startup args). 2) check OTEL_TRACES_SAMPLER env — set OTEL_TRACES_SAMPLER=always_on locally to reproduce. 3) enable DEBUG for io.opentelemetry to see propagation logs. 4) try a tiny repro toggling batch_size to 1 vs 100 to see pattern.

maya.l: we do use the agent via our k8s jvmOptions. sampler currently parentbased_traceidratio in configmap. i'll flip to always_on in dev.

sasha: example wrapping pattern that fixed this for us: 

```
Runnable r = Context.current().wrap(() -> {
  Span span = tracer.spanBuilder("process-record").startSpan();
  try (Scope s = span.makeCurrent()) {
    // process record
  } finally {
    span.end();
  }
});
executor.submit(r);
```
If you use CompletableFuture, wrap the Supplier similarly or use a ContextPropagatingExecutor. The java-instrumentation project has an executor-instrumentation module that can help auto-wrap.

rajiv.k: also watch out for sampling decision being cached at span creation time. switching sampler can change behavior but past traces may show mixed results until you redeploy.

maya.l: where's the internal trace dashboard link for this service? want to tail traces while testing.

observability-bot: Service traces: https://console.redwood.ai/observability/traces?service=batch-worker. Trace sampling config: https://console.redwood.ai/observability/configs/traces. For agent logs: https://console.redwood.ai/logs?query=otel%20java%20agent%20batch-worker

maya.l: ok ran with AlwaysOn + wrapping runnables + making spans current — missing spans dropped to ~2%. Found one more bug: we were creating a child span inside a library callback that spawned threads without inheriting context. Fixed that too.

sasha: nice. for prod, revert to parentbased with ratio but ensure entrypoint span is current before dispatching async ops. consider instrumenting the executor pool centrally so you don't have to wrap everywhere. link: https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-java-instrumentation/tree/main/instrumentation/java-concurrent

maya.l: opened PR with executor wrappers and sampler change (dev only) — pinging @eng-oncall to review sampler change before we push to staging.

rajiv.k: one more tip: if you want to see all spans in traces during debugging, temporarily set OTEL_TRACES_SAMPLER=always_on and OTEL_TRACES_SAMPLER_ARG=1.0, also set -Dotel.instrumentation.common.experimental=true if you rely on experimental hooks (check agent docs).

maya.l: thanks all — will post outcome. :thumbsup: 

maya.l: follow-up (1781234699): deployed fix to staging earlier — spans look consistent in console now, batch traces show full child spans. closing this thread, will roll to prod after canary.
